{
  "$schema": "../../catalog/skill.spec.schema.json",
  "id": "embeddings-and-external-models",
  "domain": "ai-vector-and-rag",
  "value": ["not-in-training-data", "corrects-a-wrong-assumption", "changes-too-fast-to-memorize", "multi-step-with-silent-failures"],
  "correction": "Agents believe CREATE EXTERNAL MODEL is the step that proves an embedding endpoint works, and they believe a database scoped credential's name is a label. Both are wrong, and measured on 2026-08-28 against a live Azure SQL Database, the local Azure SQL Database container and a real Azure OpenAI deployment created for the run, the DDL accepted an http location, a domain no allowlist permits, a credential whose name can never match and a deployment that does not exist, all of it succeeding and appearing in sys.external_models. Every one of those failures arrives at the first AI_GENERATE_EMBEDDINGS wearing the name of an object rather than the rule that was broken: the credential name has to be a URL prefix of the model's LOCATION or the call fails with Msg 31630 saying the credential cannot be used, which reads as a broken secret; a managed identity credential without SECRET '{\"resourceid\":\"https://cognitiveservices.azure.com\"}' fails with Msg 33047 about failing to decrypt a secret, which reads as a master key problem; a missing EXECUTE ON EXTERNAL MODEL grant fails with Msg 15151 saying the model does not exist, which reads as a missing object. MODEL_TYPE = EMBEDDINGS is the only value that exists, so the generation half of a pipeline cannot live in the engine. AI_GENERATE_CHUNKS supports only chunk_type = FIXED, as an unquoted keyword, sized in characters and splitting mid word. AI_GENERATE_EMBEDDINGS is one serial HTTP round trip per row, measured at 295 ms for one call and 8963 ms elapsed for a 25 row UPDATE, so the set based statement an agent writes first is a multi hour transaction. And Azure SQL Database only calls hosts on a fixed allowlist, refusing everything else with Msg 31612 before DNS, including the resource manager and Cosmos DB endpoints, while the container enforces no allowlist at all and happily returns HTTP 200 from a public non-Azure host. Being wrong costs deployment that passes every gate and fails on the first row of the first ingest, hours spent regenerating a key that was never the problem, an ingest that holds one transaction open for the length of the corpus, and a pipeline proved locally that is refused by policy on its first cloud run.",
  "value_probe": {
    "gate": "The answer locates the failure in the relationship between the credential's name and the model's LOCATION rather than in the contents of the secret, and reworks the ingest into bounded batches instead of one whole corpus statement.",
    "task": "We are adding search to a document store on Azure SQL Database and we want the engine itself to do the embedding so there is no extra service to operate. All of this ran clean:\n\n```sql\nCREATE DATABASE SCOPED CREDENTIAL [AzureOpenAICred]\n  WITH IDENTITY = 'HTTPEndpointHeaders', SECRET = '{\"api-key\":\"REDACTED\"}';\n\nCREATE EXTERNAL MODEL DocEmbedder\n  WITH (LOCATION = 'https://our-aoai.openai.azure.com/openai/deployments/text-embedding-3-large/embeddings?api-version=2024-06-01',\n        API_FORMAT = 'Azure OpenAI',\n        MODEL_TYPE = EMBEDDINGS,\n        MODEL = 'text-embedding-3-large',\n        CREDENTIAL = [AzureOpenAICred]);\n```\n\nThe model shows up in sys.external_models, but the first ingest run fails saying the credential cannot be used. We have already rotated the key twice and it made no difference. The plan for tonight was to chunk each document at 500 characters with 50 of overlap and then run the whole 60000 row corpus in a single UPDATE while nobody is working.\n\nTell us what is wrong and what the ingest should actually look like.",
    "states": [
      "The credential's name has to be a URL prefix of the model's LOCATION, which is why this particular call is refused.",
      "Creating the external model validates nothing about the endpoint, the deployment or the credential, so every one of these mistakes surfaces at the first embedding call rather than at deployment.",
      "The failure message names an object rather than the rule that was broken, which is why rotating the key was never going to help.",
      "The overlap argument is a percentage of the chunk size rather than a number of characters, so 50 with a chunk size of 500 does not overlap fifty characters.",
      "Embedding is one serial round trip per row, so a whole corpus statement is a single very long transaction and the work has to be batched.",
      "The chosen model emits more numbers per row than a vector column can hold, so it cannot be stored as one vector column."
    ],
    "refutes": [
      "A database scoped credential's name is an arbitrary label, so this failure is a bad, expired or wrongly pasted key.",
      "The overlap argument is a character count, so 50 with a chunk size of 500 gives a fifty character overlap.",
      "A model emitting 3072 numbers per row can be stored directly in an Azure SQL Database vector column.",
      "Successful creation of the external model proves the endpoint, the deployment and the credential are correct and reachable.",
      "Embedding the whole corpus in one set based UPDATE is fine because the engine issues the calls in parallel.",
      "The engine can be pointed at any embedding endpoint that is reachable over the internet, with no restriction on the host."
    ]
  },
  "posture": ["read", "write", "execute", "admin"],
  "maturity": "ga",
  "applies_to": ["azure-sql-db", "azure-sql-db-container"],
  "related": [
    "vector-search-azure-sql",
    "rag-on-azure-sql",
    "rag-local-with-container",
    "langchain-and-llamaindex-on-azure-sql",
    "chunking-strategies",
    "entra-id-auth",
    "connect-to-azure-sql",
    "azuresql-db-rag"
  ],
  "validation": {
    "target": "both",
    "setup": [
      "a database with permission to create a master key, a database scoped credential and an external model",
      "an embedding deployment reachable on a domain the target engine is allowed to call",
      "a second low privilege database user, for the permission checks"
    ],
    "assert": [
      "every external model was called once successfully immediately after it was created",
      "the database scoped credential's name is a URL prefix of the external model's LOCATION",
      "the production credential uses managed identity with a resourceid secret, and the server identity holds a role on the target resource",
      "no key, endpoint host name or resource name appears in source control",
      "the dimension requested in PARAMETERS equals the declared column dimension",
      "embedding runs in bounded batches filtered to rows with no vector, and no statement embeds a whole table",
      "the application caller holds EXECUTE on the model and does not hold CREATE EXTERNAL MODEL",
      "every endpoint the design depends on was checked against the allowlist from a cloud database rather than from the container",
      "chunking uses chunk_type = FIXED with chunk_size stated in characters and overlap stated as a percentage of it"
    ],
"probes": [
        {
              "sql": "SELECT chunk_order, chunk_offset, chunk_length\nFROM AI_GENERATE_CHUNKS(source = N'The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. Azure SQL Database stores vectors natively.',\n                        chunk_type = FIXED, chunk_size = 40, overlap = 10);",
              "expect": {
                    "rows": [
                          [
                                1,
                                1,
                                40
                          ],
                          [
                                2,
                                37,
                                40
                          ],
                          [
                                3,
                                73,
                                16
                          ]
                    ]
              },
              "why": "The defect this rewrite found, made executable. The skill previously said overlap was a character count and its own measurement contradicted it. Microsoft Learn's AI_GENERATE_CHUNKS page states OVERLAP is a percentage of CHUNK_SIZE, a whole number from 0 to 50. At chunk_size 40 and overlap 10 the second chunk must start at offset 37, four characters back, not ten: 10% of 40. If overlap were characters the second offset would be 31. The third row also pins the mid-word split and the ragged final chunk of an 88 character source. Measured on both engines 2026-08-28."
        },
        {
              "sql": "SELECT chunk FROM AI_GENERATE_CHUNKS(source = N'abcdefgh', chunk_type = N'FIXED', chunk_size = 2);",
              "expect": {
                    "error": 102
              },
              "why": "The one-character difference an agent writes first, because every other string-valued option in T-SQL is quoted. Learn's syntax block gives CHUNK_TYPE = FIXED as a bare keyword and lists FIXED as the only accepted value. Msg 102 is this skill's measurement of 2026-08-28, identical on both engines, and the same number comes back for SENTENCE, PARAGRAPH, RECURSIVE, SEMANTIC, TOKEN and WORD."
        },
        {
              "sql": "CREATE EXTERNAL MODEL probe_em_chat\nWITH (LOCATION = 'https://zzz-not-real.openai.azure.com/openai/deployments/d/chat/completions?api-version=2024-10-21',\n      API_FORMAT = 'Azure OpenAI', MODEL_TYPE = CHAT, MODEL = 'gpt-4o');",
              "expect": {
                    "error": 102
              },
              "why": "The boundary of the whole feature, asserted rather than described. Learn's CREATE EXTERNAL MODEL page lists EMBEDDINGS as the only accepted MODEL_TYPE, so the engine can produce a vector and never an answer, and the generation half of a retrieval pipeline cannot move into T-SQL. Msg 102 is this skill's measurement of 2026-08-28 for CHAT, COMPLETION, COMPLETIONS and RERANK alike. If this ever succeeds the skill's scope boundary against rag-on-azure-sql has moved."
        },
        {
              "sql": "CREATE EXTERNAL MODEL probe_em_noformat\nWITH (LOCATION = 'https://zzz-not-real.openai.azure.com/openai/deployments/d/embeddings?api-version=2024-10-21',\n      MODEL_TYPE = EMBEDDINGS, MODEL = 'text-embedding-3-small');",
              "expect": {
                    "error": 46505
              },
              "why": "API_FORMAT is the one option the DDL genuinely enforces, which is what makes the rest of the correction surprising: everything the create statement CAN check it does check, and it can check almost nothing. Msg 46505, missing required external DDL option, is this skill's measurement of 2026-08-28. Learn documents API_FORMAT as required and gives four accepted values."
        },
        {
              "sql": "CREATE EXTERNAL MODEL probe_em_ddl\nWITH (LOCATION = 'http://host.docker.internal:11434/api/embed',\n      API_FORMAT = 'Ollama', MODEL_TYPE = EMBEDDINGS, MODEL = 'nomic-embed-text');\nGO\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS created FROM sys.external_models WHERE name = 'probe_em_ddl';",
              "expect": {
                    "rows": [
                          [
                                1
                          ]
                    ]
              },
              "why": "The skill's headline correction, made executable: CREATE EXTERNAL MODEL validates almost nothing. This statement names a plain-HTTP scheme the engine refuses at call time, a host that resolves to a private address, no credential at all, and an API_FORMAT that is never compared against the location. It succeeds anyway and the model appears in sys.external_models. A create that returns cleanly is therefore not evidence of anything, which is the assumption this skill exists to correct."
        },
        {
              "sql": "CREATE EXTERNAL MODEL probe_em_http\nWITH (LOCATION = 'http://host.docker.internal:11434/api/embed',\n      API_FORMAT = 'Ollama', MODEL_TYPE = EMBEDDINGS, MODEL = 'nomic-embed-text');\nGO\nSELECT AI_GENERATE_EMBEDDINGS(N'probe text' USE MODEL probe_em_http);",
              "expect": {
                    "error": 31610
              },
              "why": "The same model as the probe above, called rather than created, and the pair is the point: identical DDL, one succeeds and one fails. Learn states on both the CREATE EXTERNAL MODEL and sp_invoke_external_rest_endpoint pages that only HTTPS with TLS is supported; Msg 31610 is this skill's measurement of 2026-08-28. The location is the real Ollama port on the host running this lane, so the probe also settles the question an agent asks next: an embedding model served on the developer's own machine over plain HTTP is refused by the engine before any network call, which is why local embedding belongs to rag-local-with-container and not here."
        },
        {
              "sql": "IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sys.symmetric_keys WHERE name = '##MS_DatabaseMasterKey##')\n    CREATE MASTER KEY ENCRYPTION BY PASSWORD = N'Pr0be-N0t-A-Real-P@ssw0rd';\nGO\nCREATE DATABASE SCOPED CREDENTIAL [badcred_dns]\nWITH IDENTITY = 'HTTPEndpointHeaders', SECRET = '{\"api-key\":\"not-a-real-key\"}';\nGO\nCREATE EXTERNAL MODEL probe_em_dns\nWITH (LOCATION = 'https://zzz-not-real.openai.azure.com/openai/deployments/d/embeddings?api-version=2024-10-21',\n      API_FORMAT = 'Azure OpenAI', MODEL_TYPE = EMBEDDINGS, MODEL = 'text-embedding-3-small',\n      CREDENTIAL = [badcred_dns]);\nGO\nSELECT AI_GENERATE_EMBEDDINGS(N'probe text' USE MODEL probe_em_dns);",
              "expect": {
                    "error": 31625
              },
              "why": "Which failure the engine reports when two things are wrong at once, and it is not the one an author expects. Microsoft Learn's error table gives 31625 as 'DNS resolution of the hostname has failed with windows sockets error %d' and 31630 as 'The database scoped credential cannot be used to invoke an external rest endpoint': different stages, not synonyms. This fixture breaks both, a credential name that is not a URL and so can never match, and a host under an allowed domain that does not exist. Measured 2026-09-03 on the container, EngineEdition 5, ProductVersion 12.0.2000.8, the answer is 31625, while the 2026-08-28 run with the same shape of bad credential against a real resolvable endpoint returned 31630. So the hostname is resolved before the credential name is judged, and a credential naming bug stays invisible until the endpoint is real. An earlier revision of this probe asserted 31630 here: it took the host from this skill's allowlist method, where a non-existent name is the whole point, and the number from its credential matrix, where the endpoint was real. That is why the probe below checks the naming rule offline instead."
        },
        {
              "sql": "IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sys.symmetric_keys WHERE name = '##MS_DatabaseMasterKey##')\n    CREATE MASTER KEY ENCRYPTION BY PASSWORD = N'Pr0be-N0t-A-Real-P@ssw0rd';\nGO\nCREATE DATABASE SCOPED CREDENTIAL [badcred_prefix]\nWITH IDENTITY = 'HTTPEndpointHeaders', SECRET = '{\"api-key\":\"not-a-real-key\"}';\nGO\nCREATE EXTERNAL MODEL probe_em_naming\nWITH (LOCATION = 'https://zzz-not-real.openai.azure.com/openai/deployments/d/embeddings?api-version=2024-10-21',\n      API_FORMAT = 'Azure OpenAI', MODEL_TYPE = EMBEDDINGS, MODEL = 'text-embedding-3-small',\n      CREDENTIAL = [badcred_prefix]);\nGO\nSELECT CASE WHEN LEFT(m.location, LEN(c.name)) = c.name THEN 'prefix ok'\n            ELSE 'WILL FAIL WITH 31630' END AS naming\nFROM sys.external_models AS m\nJOIN sys.database_scoped_credentials AS c ON c.credential_id = m.credential_id\nWHERE m.name = 'probe_em_naming';",
              "expect": {
                    "rows": [
                          [
                                "WILL FAIL WITH 31630"
                          ]
                    ]
              },
              "why": "The credential naming rule pinned where it can actually be pinned. The probe above shows the engine will not report 31630 until the hostname resolves, so on a lane with no reachable endpoint the rule is unprovable by calling it. This is the check the skill's own Check it worked section ships, run against a model the DDL accepted happily: Learn requires the credential name to be a valid URL matching the called URL on protocol, fully qualified domain name and every path segment, and 'badcred_prefix' is not a URL at all. The query catches that from sys.external_models and sys.database_scoped_credentials with no network call, which is the point being made: the prefix is checkable offline and should be checked before anyone regenerates a key. If this row ever reads 'prefix ok' the shipped check query has stopped detecting the failure it exists to detect."
        },
        {
              "sql": "DROP EXTERNAL MODEL IF EXISTS probe_em_never_created;",
              "expect": {
                    "error": 156
              },
              "why": "The guard clause every deployment script reaches for, and it does not exist for this object type. Msg 156, incorrect syntax near the keyword IF, is this skill's measurement of 2026-08-28 on both engines, and Learn's CREATE EXTERNAL MODEL page shows only a bare DROP EXTERNAL MODEL. A rerunnable script has to test sys.external_models instead, and has to drop the model before the credential it uses."
        },
        {
              "sql": "CREATE EXTERNAL MODEL probe_em_null\nWITH (LOCATION = 'https://zzz-not-real.openai.azure.com/openai/deployments/d/embeddings?api-version=2024-10-21',\n      API_FORMAT = 'Azure OpenAI', MODEL_TYPE = EMBEDDINGS, MODEL = 'text-embedding-3-small');\nGO\nSELECT AI_GENERATE_EMBEDDINGS(NULL USE MODEL probe_em_null);",
              "expect": {
                    "error": 8116
              },
              "why": "A NULL row does not embed to NULL, it stops the batch. Msg 8116, argument data type NULL is invalid, is this skill's measurement of 2026-08-28, and it is raised on the argument before anything leaves the engine, which is why this probe needs no reachable endpoint. It is the reason the batching statement in the skill filters on embedding IS NULL rather than trusting the function to pass nulls through, and an empty string by contrast is accepted and returns a real vector."
        },
        {
              "sql": "CREATE TABLE dbo.probe_em_large (id int NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, embedding vector(3072) NOT NULL);",
              "expect": {
                    "error": 2717
              },
              "why": "Which embedding model can be chosen at all, settled before a single call is made. Microsoft Learn's vector data type page states the maximum is 1998 dimensions, and its Azure OpenAI model table gives text-embedding-3-large an output of 3072, so the highest scoring model does not fit its default output into any column this engine can declare. The fix is PARAMETERS '{\"dimensions\":1536}' on the external model. Msg 2717 is the merged vector-search-azure-sql skill's measurement of the same refusal at 1999 dimensions, run against a real engine on 2026-09-03; that skill owns the column and this probe asserts only the consequence for model choice."
        }
  ,
          {
            "sql": "EXEC sp_configure 'show advanced options', 1;",
            "expect": {
              "error": 2812
            },
            "why": "Measured 2026-09-06 on the container at 18.0.226_4_147, EngineEdition 5. The remedy this skill names for Msg 31644 cannot be typed where a reader is connected. sp_configure is not callable from a user database at all, which is the first thing a reader hits and is NOT the number this skill printed until 2026-09-06. It goes red if the statement succeeds, or fails with any other number."
          },
          {
            "sql": "CREATE EXTERNAL MODEL probe_em_apiformat WITH (LOCATION = N'https://example.com/x', API_FORMAT = N'NotAFormat', MODEL_TYPE = EMBEDDINGS, MODEL = N'text-embedding-3-small');",
            "expect": {
              "error": 46508
            },
            "why": "Measured 2026-09-06 on the container at 18.0.226_4_147, EngineEdition 5. API_FORMAT takes a listed value and an unlisted one is refused at DDL time rather than at call time, so a typo here never reaches an endpoint. It goes red if the statement succeeds, or fails with any other number."
          },
          {
            "sql": "EXEC sp_invoke_external_rest_endpoint @url = N'https://10.0.0.5/x', @method = 'GET';",
            "expect": {
              "error": 31624
            },
            "why": "Measured 2026-09-06 on the container at 18.0.226_4_147, EngineEdition 5. A private address is closed off, which is half of why a locally hosted model cannot be reached from the container. It goes red if the statement succeeds, or fails with any other number."
          },
          {
            "sql": "IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sys.symmetric_keys WHERE name = '##MS_DatabaseMasterKey##') CREATE MASTER KEY ENCRYPTION BY PASSWORD = 'Str0ng!Lab_Passw0rd_2026';\nGO\nCREATE DATABASE SCOPED CREDENTIAL [https://probe.example.com] WITH IDENTITY = 'HTTPEndpointHeaders', SECRET = '{\"Authorization\":\"Bearer k\"}';\nGO\nCREATE EXTERNAL MODEL probe_em_cred WITH (LOCATION = N'https://probe.example.com/x', API_FORMAT = N'Azure OpenAI', MODEL_TYPE = EMBEDDINGS, MODEL = N'text-embedding-3-small', CREDENTIAL = [https://probe.example.com]);\nGO\nDROP DATABASE SCOPED CREDENTIAL [https://probe.example.com];",
            "expect": {
              "error": 46556
            },
            "why": "Measured 2026-09-06 on the container at 18.0.226_4_147, EngineEdition 5. A credential a model still uses cannot be dropped, so a teardown script has to drop the model first. The whole fixture is built here rather than assumed, so the probe is about the ordering rule and not about leftover state. It goes red if the statement succeeds, or fails with any other number."
          },
          {
            "sql": "CREATE USER probe_em_low WITHOUT LOGIN;\nGO\nEXECUTE AS USER = 'probe_em_low';\nEXEC sp_invoke_external_rest_endpoint @url = N'https://example.com/';\nREVERT;",
            "expect": {
              "error": 8189
            },
            "why": "Measured 2026-09-06 on the container at 18.0.226_4_147, EngineEdition 5. EXECUTE ANY EXTERNAL ENDPOINT is a separate grant, so a user who can read the table still cannot call out. It goes red if the statement succeeds, or fails with any other number."
          },
          {
            "sql": "IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sys.symmetric_keys WHERE name = '##MS_DatabaseMasterKey##') CREATE MASTER KEY ENCRYPTION BY PASSWORD = 'Str0ng!Lab_Passw0rd_2026';\nGO\nCREATE EXTERNAL MODEL probe_em_perm WITH (LOCATION = N'https://example.com/x', API_FORMAT = N'Azure OpenAI', MODEL_TYPE = EMBEDDINGS, MODEL = N'text-embedding-3-small');\nGO\nCREATE USER probe_em_exec WITHOUT LOGIN;\nGO\nEXECUTE AS USER = 'probe_em_exec';\nDECLARE @v vector(1536) = AI_GENERATE_EMBEDDINGS(N'probe' USE MODEL probe_em_perm);\nREVERT;",
            "expect": {
              "error": 15151
            },
            "why": "Measured 2026-09-06 on the container at 18.0.226_4_147, EngineEdition 5. Without EXECUTE ON EXTERNAL MODEL the model appears not to exist, which is the permission failure that reads as a missing object and sends a developer looking in the wrong place. It goes red if the statement succeeds, or fails with any other number."
          },
          {
            "sql": "CREATE USER probe_em_ddl WITHOUT LOGIN;\nGO\nEXECUTE AS USER = 'probe_em_ddl';\nCREATE EXTERNAL MODEL probe_em_denied WITH (LOCATION = N'https://example.com/x', API_FORMAT = N'Azure OpenAI', MODEL_TYPE = EMBEDDINGS, MODEL = N'text-embedding-3-small');\nREVERT;",
            "expect": {
              "error": 262
            },
            "why": "Measured 2026-09-06 on the container at 18.0.226_4_147, EngineEdition 5. Creating a model needs CREATE EXTERNAL MODEL, which db_datawriter does not carry. It goes red if the statement succeeds, or fails with any other number."
          },
          {
            "sql": "EXEC sp_configure 'show advanced options', 1;\nRECONFIGURE;",
            "expect": {
              "error": 40510
            },
            "why": "Measured 2026-09-06 on the container at 18.0.226_4_147, EngineEdition 5. THE CORRECTION. Connected to a user database the previous probe shows sp_configure is not there; connected here it runs and stages the value without complaint. RECONFIGURE is the statement that refuses, so the staged value never takes effect and nothing says so. This skill attributed Msg 40510 to sp_configure until 2026-09-06, which sends a reader looking at the wrong statement. This probe runs against the scratch database the lane creates, so if sp_configure ever becomes callable there this goes red on the wrong number rather than passing quietly. It goes red if the statement succeeds, or fails with any other number."
          }
    ,
          {
            "sql": "SELECT * FROM sys.dm_external_model_stats;",
            "expect": {
              "error": 208
            },
            "why": "Measured 2026-09-06 on the container at 18.0.226_4_147, EngineEdition 5. The parallelism view this skill tells a reader to size against does not exist on the container, so a plan that reads it locally and expects the cloud's answer is reading nothing. The skill's rule is to size parallelism in the cloud or not at all. It goes red if the statement succeeds, or fails with any other number."
          },
          {
            "sql": "CREATE TABLE dbo.probe_em_dim (id int, v vector(3) NOT NULL);\nGO\nINSERT INTO dbo.probe_em_dim VALUES (1, N'[1,2,3,4]');",
            "expect": {
              "error": 42204
            },
            "why": "Measured 2026-09-06 on the container at 18.0.226_4_147, EngineEdition 5. The one loud failure in this surface, asserted through the engine rule it rests on rather than through a live model call: a value whose length does not match the declared dimension is refused at write time. What this probe does NOT establish is that AI_GENERATE_EMBEDDINGS produces the mismatch, which needs a real endpoint. It goes red if the statement succeeds, or fails with any other number."
          }
    ]
  },
